        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Mehrgarh culture</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Homeland</span><span class="info-stat-val">The Kacchi Plain of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balochistan">Balochistan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a>, near the Bolan Pass, west of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indus">Indus River</a>, between Quetta, Kalat and Sibi; six mounds on a site of about 2 km²; the Sibri cemetery about 8 km away</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">Period I (aceramic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neolithic">Neolithic</a>) 5250–4650 BCE by recent radiocarbon dating, formerly pre-7000–5500 BCE; Period II 4650–4000 BCE; Period III (Chalcolithic, Togau phase) 4000–3500 BCE; Periods IV–VI 3500–3000 BCE; Period VII 2600–2000 BCE; Period VIII at Sibri</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">early farming of barley and wheat; herding of sheep, goats and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a>; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mudbrick">mud-brick</a> houses and granaries; drilled teeth (proto-dentistry); female clay figurines; wheel-made Togau pottery with geometric designs; button seals; the oldest known lost-wax casting</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">How we know them</span><span class="info-stat-val">Excavations by the French Archaeological Mission in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indus">Indus</a> Basin (1974–1986 and 1997–2000), about 32,000 artefacts; radiocarbon dates, including on teeth; dental studies of the burials; genetic studies of lactose tolerance in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a></span></div>
